{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.EulerMaclaurinFirst","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.EulerMaclaurinFirst","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.MeanValue","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals.Basic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.grid_defect_bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.grid_defect_bracket","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/EulerMaclaurinFirst.lean#L146-L189","doc":"**First Euler–Maclaurin correction on a uniform grid.**  For `f` with\nantitone derivative on `[0, nh]`, the right-endpoint Riemann defect is\nbracketed by `h²/2` times the two endpoint Riemann sums of `f′`:\n\n    (h²/2)·Σ_{i<n} f′(x_{i+1})  ≤  Σ_{i<n} ∫_{cell_i} (f(x_{i+1}) − f(u)) du\n                                ≤  (h²/2)·Σ_{i<n} f′(x_i).\n\nBoth envelopes are `(h/2)` times a Riemann sum of `f′` over `[0, nh]`, so\nboth converge to `(h/2)·(f(nh) − f(0))` — the first Euler–Maclaurin term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.cell_defect_bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.cell_defect_bracket","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/EulerMaclaurinFirst.lean#L103-L144","doc":"**First Euler–Maclaurin correction, per cell.**  For `f` with antitone\nderivative on the cell `[a, a+h]`, the right-endpoint defect is bracketed\nby `h²/2` times the endpoint derivatives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.integral_sub_linear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.integral_sub_linear","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/EulerMaclaurinFirst.lean#L93-L101","doc":"`∫_a^{a+h} (a + h − u) du = h²/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.sub_bracket_of_antitoneOn_deriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.sub_bracket_of_antitoneOn_deriv","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/EulerMaclaurinFirst.lean#L63-L91","doc":"The mean-value bracket for an antitone derivative: on `u ≤ b`,\n`(b−u)·f′(b) ≤ f b − f u ≤ (b−u)·f′(u)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}